   "source": [
    "# Code Smell Detection using Weave and LiteLLM\n",
    "\n",
    "Detecting code smells—patterns indicating design problems—is crucial for maintaining software quality. This guide demonstrates an end-to-end pipeline for identifying and evaluating code smells in a Java codebase.\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use Weave for tracking, versioning, and evaluating our pipeline, and `litellm` to interact with language models for analysis and evaluation."
   ],
   "id": "dfb52a9e5385022b"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why use Weave?\n",
    "\n",
    "In this tutorial, we'll use Weave to implement and evaluate our code smell detection pipeline. You'll learn how to:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Track your LLM pipeline**: Log inputs, outputs, and intermediate steps of the analysis and evaluation process.\n",
    "2. **Evaluate LLM outputs**: Create and compare evaluations of the detected code smells against a ground truth dataset."
   ],
   "id": "50d20397d41a7c4d"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
